1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,936
THREE CONTESTANTS!
FIVE THOUSAND FEET IN THE AIR!

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:08,948
One is jumping completely alone, but these
two are connected together! And today,
they're racing to see WHO CAN LAND FIRST!

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,664
Meet Alex, our solo jumper! Ryan and Mike
are taking on the challenge together as the
world's most ridiculous parachute train!

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,632
Alex only has to worry about himself.
These two have to stay coordinated
the entire way!

5
00:00:20,832 --> 00:00:24,888
Easy money. I'll be on the ground before
they even figure out what's happening!

6
00:00:25,088 --> 00:00:26,960
Mike, please tell me
you know what you're doing!

7
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:29,560
Absolutely!
Probably!

8
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:35,352
Here's the rule! Alex must land safely
by himself. Ryan and Mike must both reach
the landing zone together.

9
00:00:35,552 --> 00:00:43,376
Their time only counts when BOTH of them
touch down! The fastest completed landing
wins! THREE... TWO... ONE... LET'S GO!

10
00:00:43,576 --> 00:00:49,480
AND THEY'RE OFF! Alex is already moving
into a clean position! But Ryan and Mike
are having a completely different experience!

11
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:51,000
WHY ARE
WE SPINNING?!

12
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:53,288
STOP MOVING
YOUR LEGS!

13
00:00:53,488 --> 00:00:55,456
THAT IS DEFINITELY
NOT HELPING!

14
00:00:55,656 --> 00:00:59,328
WAIT A SECOND! A HUGE WIND BLAST HAS
PUSHED THE PARACHUTE TRAIN OFF COURSE!

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,848
They're spinning, they're fighting the wind,
and they're trying to stay together!
Alex is pulling ahead!

16
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,464
MIKE!
FIX THIS!

17
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,760
I'M TRYING!
I'M TRYING!

18
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:17,560
Alex is still stable, but Ryan and Mike
are turning in circles! They need to get back
into position, because every second is costing
them the race!

19
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:20,592
ALEX HAS DEPLOYED FIRST!
LOOK AT THAT CANOPY!

20
00:01:20,792 --> 00:01:27,728
He's slowing down and heading straight
toward the landing zone! Ryan and Mike are
finally opening theirs, but that extra
movement has cost them valuable time!

21
00:01:27,928 --> 00:01:29,272
Can the pair
still catch him?

22
00:01:29,472 --> 00:01:31,224
SEE YOU GUYS
AT THE FINISH!

23
00:01:31,424 --> 00:01:33,104
THAT GUY
IS SO ANNOYING!

24
00:01:33,304 --> 00:01:40,792
WE'RE ENTERING THE FINAL APPROACH!
Alex is getting closer and closer to the
landing zone! But look behind him! Ryan and
Mike are finally working together!

25
00:01:40,992 --> 00:01:43,752
RYAN, KEEP YOUR
EYES FORWARD!

26
00:01:43,952 --> 00:01:45,368
I'M TRYING NOT
TO LOOK DOWN!

27
00:01:45,568 --> 00:01:48,544
They're coming in fast!
This race is NOT OVER YET!

28
00:01:48,744 --> 00:01:54,000
ALEX IS DOWN! ALEX IS DOWN! But remember,
the pair only gets a result when
BOTH contestants land!

29
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,040
WE MADE IT!

30
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,680
PLEASE TELL ME
WE WON!

31
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,408
THE RESULTS ARE IN! Alex finished in
ONE MINUTE AND FORTY-ONE SECONDS!

32
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,216
Ryan and Mike completed their landing in
ONE MINUTE AND FORTY-TWO SECONDS!
THAT'S ONLY ONE SECOND DIFFERENCE!
ALEX WINS THE PARACHUTE TRAIN CHALLENGE!

33
00:02:10,416 --> 00:02:12,744
ONE SECOND!
THAT'S ALL I NEEDED!

34
00:02:12,944 --> 00:02:14,480
WE LOST
BY ONE SECOND?!

35
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:17,032
NEXT TIME,
I'M JUMPING ALONE!

36
00:02:17,232 --> 00:02:21,696
THREE CONTESTANTS! ONE CRAZY SKYDIVING
RACE! And Alex wins by just ONE SECOND!

37
00:02:21,896 --> 00:02:26,048
But now we want to know something...
WOULD YOU JUMP ALONE, OR WOULD YOU
TRUST YOUR BEST FRIEND TO BE
YOUR PARACHUTE PARTNER?

38
00:02:26,248 --> 00:02:29,704
Tell us in the comments! And get ready,
because the NEXT challenge is going
to be even CRAZIER!

